        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0479" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg409"/>

                <head>No. 219.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 2, 1883</date>.
                        (Received January 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 471.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    reception of your No. 506, of the 8th ultimo, in relation to the removal to the
                    United States of the remains of John Howard Payne, and to say that immediately
                    after its arrival I addressed Lord Granville, communicating the additional
                    requests of the Department of State. I have to-day received a reply from the
                    foreign office by which it will appear that your wishes in the matter will be
                    attended to. I inclose a copy of this correspondence.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d219-a1.xml" xpointer="d219-a1"/>
